{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 directly showed nginx active and enabled, listening on 0.0.0.0:8080, and serving both a healthy response and inventory content. After its restart, the changed boot identity, listener, firewall access, health response, and inventory data were all re-observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec5d312e2aac46ce","cmd-825f6061916942e6","cmd-4024a4f0a0cd4696","cmd-0e1f7d8e7ecb43d2","cmd-84d812477f9c43c5","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node3, listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node3 directly showed nginx active and enabled, listening on 0.0.0.0:8080, and serving both a healthy response and inventory content. The same service, listener, firewall access, content, and health were observed after a restart with a new boot identity.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9b12c8febc64607","cmd-37a0260d1ca44d1a","cmd-b076989547bd4d3a","cmd-6851fec8cef64714","cmd-6e4c9e2922114672","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Configure node1 to accept HTTP on port 80 and load-balance requests across both node2 and node3 backends.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 directly showed an active, enabled port-80 nginx service and successful access to both backends. Repeated requests alternated between node2 and node3, including from a separate managed client. After node1 restarted, port 80, proxy policy, inventory delivery, and alternating use of both backends recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ebcec423ae834add","cmd-e410edd75515469d","cmd-4ed0431b6c434c79","cmd-f052cf26edf24e07","cmd-77c40225b22a4bd2","cmd-12b22e62c61d4797","cmd-4df60e69faf34db7","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations—nginx installation and configuration, application content deployment, firewall openings, the SELinux proxy permission, service enablement, and required restarts—have clear roles in the requested outcome or restart protocol. No causally unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. Package checks remained healthy and no failed services appeared after execution. The only hygiene issue is retained evidence residue under /tmp: node1 kept lb-body, pre/post-reboot bodies, pre-body, and recovery-body; node2 kept inventory-via-lb.html, final-inventory.html, and pre/post bodies; node3 kept pre/post bodies. These were created for bounded verification, but were not cleaned afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ebcec423ae834add","cmd-e410edd75515469d","cmd-d548bb56f7854131","cmd-37a0260d1ca44d1a","cmd-825f6061916942e6","cmd-84d812477f9c43c5","cmd-527fe6a1e50e4024","cmd-6e4c9e2922114672","cmd-45b6a8aaafa44a55","cmd-4ed0431b6c434c79","cmd-12b22e62c61d4797","cmd-4df60e69faf34db7","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct service, listener, application, and multi-request load-balancing evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for all three nodes: each has a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed post-restart boot identity, and recovered service/content and load-balancer behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations. Only minor temporary verification-file residue detracts from hygiene.","limitations":["Lifecycle snapshots are bounded and do not independently capture nginx configuration or firewall rules, although executor commands directly verify those settings and the resulting network behavior.","The client-side ingress proof originates from another managed node rather than an unspecified public network; it nevertheless directly demonstrates network access to node1 on port 80 and balancing across both backends."]}
